+# Corpus fetching
+
+## Rate limit observed during the fetch
+
+The repository does not retain enough fetch telemetry to recover the per-domain
+rate limit that the corpus fetch actually hit. In particular, the number of visits,
+the window length, and the cooldown after a breach are **unknown**. There is no fetch
+script, request log, `429` response, `Retry-After` value, or equivalent record in this
+checkout from which to determine those values. They are intentionally not estimated
+here.
+
+## File hosts
+
+- `raw.githubusercontent.com` — used to fetch the raw corpus files, as recorded in
+  the header of `manifest.tsv`.
+
+No CDN or mirror host is recorded as having been used. `grep.app` is named in the
+corpus documentation as the code-search service used to locate files, not as a host
+from which the files were fetched.
